blaze_face_short_range.tflite
=============================

MediaPipe Face Detector — BlazeFace (short range) model.

Source:  https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/face_detector/
         blaze_face_short_range/float16/1/blaze_face_short_range.tflite
Author:  Google LLC (MediaPipe)
License: Apache License 2.0

This model file is redistributed unmodified under the terms of the Apache
License, Version 2.0. A copy of that licence is available at:

    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Apache-2.0 is compatible with this application's AGPL-3.0-or-later licence
and carries no field-of-use restriction, which is why it was chosen over
the alternatives. Google ML Kit's face detector was rejected for exactly
that reason: it ships as a proprietary binary blob and could not be built
from source, which would have made the app ineligible for F-Droid and
would have broken the promise that every part of Тахь can be inspected and
rebuilt by the people who rely on it.

What the model does, and what it does not
----------------------------------------

It reports where human faces appear in an image. It does not identify
anyone, it does not compare a face to any other face, and it does not know
whose face it is looking at. The application uses it for one purpose only:
to refuse a driver portrait that contains no person — a photograph of a
mountain, a car, a logo or a cartoon.

No image ever leaves the device. Inference runs locally against this
bundled file; there is no network call in the portrait pipeline, and
`test/profile/driver_photo_offline_test.dart` enforces that mechanically.
